<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="34675" href="schedule/2007/spring/IB/496/34675.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2007" href="schedule/2007.xml">2007</calendarYear><term id="120071" href="schedule/2007/spring.xml">Spring 2007</term><subject id="IB" href="schedule/2007/spring/IB.xml">Integrative Biology</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2007/spring/IB/496.xml">Special Courses</course></parents><sectionNumber>CKA</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>College-Level Biology Teaching</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This seminar is for graduate students interested in teaching biology at the college/university level.  Its purpose is to help you to make the transition to being a professor.  We will read literature to help make you aware of the scholarship of teaching and learning and to give you ideas about how to implement best practices in your classroom.  Ultimately, we aim for you to develop a personal philosophy and style to serve as a basis for your academic career.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2007-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2007-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>04:30 PM</start><end>05:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>176</roomNumber><buildingName>Burrill Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Augspurger" firstName="C">Augspurger, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>